  "notes": [
    "An initial ES module wrapper retained CommonJS registration, which Vitest rejected. Replacing that registration with the ESM export fixed the integration; embedded WASM is unchanged.",
    "The long-clip browser study initially assumed the file sample rate. The browser decoded to 44.1 kHz; the assertion now uses the actual decoded frame count.",
    "The native study had a syntax typo and one invocation omitted its required mode argument; both were corrected before retaining results.",
    "The first clean-check command had an unquoted PATH containing Windows directories with spaces and never started npm; the quoted command completed the full sequence.",
    "After this implementation commit, the final source commit adds documentation and evidence only.",
    "Headless audio rendering and pitch measurements are not human listening or physical microphone validation."
  ],
  "scope": "Local clean web build and source evidence; no package release or hosted deployment."
